  "term": "relay nucleus",
  "definition": "A relay nucleus is a thalamic nucleus that passes activity on to the cortical module in thalamo-cortico-thalamic circuitry. In this packet, it refers to the thalamic relay nucleus as part of the pathway linking thalamus and cortex.",
